WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.560
Mom was losing her short-term memory,

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.890
but&nbsp;was better recalling
 her younger years.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.640
I'd ask, and she would tell me stories.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.225
I&nbsp;listened, and I was her audience.

00:00:12.957 --> 00:00:17.246
I got ideas. I wrote them down, 
and I sketched them out.

00:00:17.865 --> 00:00:21.668
I showed&nbsp;her what to do by 
acting out the scenarios myself.

00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:24.451
We would then stage them.

00:00:25.385 --> 00:00:28.000
So she posed,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.476
and I learned more 
about photography.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:36.221
Mom loved the process, the acting.

00:00:36.221 --> 00:00:40.148
She felt&nbsp;worthy again, she 
felt wanted and needed.

00:00:40.961 --> 00:00:43.800
With any Alzheimer's, dementia, there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.505 --> 00:00:48.412
a certain amount of frustration 
and sadness&nbsp;for everyone involved.

00:00:48.412 --> 00:00:51.608
But to balance off all 
the difficulties, we played.

00:00:51.608 --> 00:00:54.012
That was Mom's&nbsp;happy place.

00:00:54.012 --> 00:00:56.347
And I needed her to be there, too.

